// The roof and attic over the trusses, in building coordinates: laminated asphalt shingles on a
// synthetic underlayment on 7/16 in OSB sheathing, a ridge vent over a 2 in slot at the ridge, 2x6
// fascia on the truss tails, vented aluminum soffits closed at the gables by stucco returns, the
// second-floor ceiling (1/2 in gypsum under the bottom chords) and R-38 blown fiberglass over it,
// bay by bay between the trusses. A polystyrene baffle in every bay keeps a 1 1/2 in air channel
// under the sheathing from the soffit vents past the insulation (DESIGN-NOTES, "Roof and attic").
// Roof layers are drawn at their nominal thickness normal to the 6:12 slope.
